{
  "dom_id": "step-71812",
  "name": "Constant Terms",
  "problem": "The **constant terms** of a linear expression are terms that contain no variables.\n\nFor example, in the expression\n\n$$\n3x + {\\color{blue}{2}} -3y +{\\color{blue}{9}},\n$$\n\nthe constant terms are ${\\color{blue}{2}}$ and ${\\color{blue}{9}}.$",
